  content: ## 🎯 Beginner C Programming Projects

This module contains complete beginner-level C programming projects that demonstrate practical applications of the concepts learned in previous modules. Each project includes detailed explanations, complete source code, and step-by-step implementation guides to help you understand how to approach and build these applications from scratch.

## 🎯 Development Approach for Beginner Projects

``` How to Approach C Programming Projects:

1. **Planning Phase:**
   - Define the problem and requirements clearly
   - Break down the functionality into smaller functions
   - Identify the data structures and algorithms needed
   - Plan the program flow and user interaction

2. **Implementation Phase:**
   - Start with basic structure (main function, includes)
   - Implement helper functions one by one
   - Test each component as you build
   - Handle errors and edge cases

3. **Testing Phase:**
   - Test normal operation scenarios
   - Test error conditions and invalid inputs
   - Verify memory management (no leaks)
   - Get feedback and iterate

4. **Documentation Phase:**
   - Add comments explaining complex logic
   - Document function purposes and parameters
   - Include usage examples

## Project 1: Number Guessing Game

``` 🎯 Project Overview
**Description:** A simple interactive game where the computer generates a random number and the player tries to guess it with hints.

**Learning Objectives:**
- Understand random number generation in C
- Practice input validation and error handling
- Implement game loops and state management
- Use functions to organize code

``` 📋 Implementation Steps

**Step 1: Plan the Game Logic**
- Generate a random number between 1-100
- Accept user guesses with validation
- Provide feedback (too high/low)
- Track number of attempts
- Allow replay functionality

**Step 2: Set Up Project Structure**
- Include necessary headers (<stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <time.h>, <stdbool.h>)
- Declare function prototypes
- Implement main game loop

**Step 3: Implement Core Functions**
- Random number generation with proper seeding
- Input validation with error recovery
- Hint system with clear feedback
- Game state management

**Concepts Used:**
- Variables and data types (##, ##)
- Control structures (while/do-while loops, if-else)
- Random number generation (#()#, #()#)
- User input/output (#()#, #()#)
- Function decomposition and modular design

**Features:**
- Random number generation between 1-100
- Input validation with error messages
- Guess counter and performance feedback
- Play again functionality with clean restart

``` 🔧 Implementation Guide

**Random Number Generation:**
```
// Always seed the random number generator once at program start
srand(time(NULL));  // Use current time as seed

// Generate random number in range [min, max]
int generate_random_number(int min, int max) {
    return rand() % (max - min + 1) + min;
}
```
**Why #(time(NULL))#?** Without seeding, #()# always produces the same sequence. #(NULL)# provides a different seed each run.

**Input Validation Strategy:**
```
// Robust input handling with error recovery
do {
    printf("Enter your guess (1-100): ");
    if (scanf("%d", &guess) == 1) {
        if (guess >= 1 && guess <= 100) {
            valid = true;
        } else {
            printf("❌ Please enter a number between 1 and 100.\\n");
        }
    } else {
        printf("❌ Invalid input. Please enter a number.\\n");
        while (getchar() != '\\n'); // Clear invalid input
    }
} while (!valid);
```
**Key Points:** Check #()# return value, validate range, clear input buffer on errors.

**Game Loop Design:**
```
do {
    // Generate new target
    // Reset guess counter
    // Play one round
} while (play_again()); // Allow replay
```
**Benefits:** Clean separation of game rounds, easy restart logic.

```#
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <time.h>
#include <stdbool.h>

// Function prototypes
int generate_random_number(int min, int max);
int get_user_guess(void);
void display_hint(int guess, int target);
bool play_again(void);

int main() {
    printf("🎯 Welcome to the Number Guessing Game!\\n");
    printf("I'm thinking of a number between 1 and 100.\\n\\n");

    // Seed random number generator
    srand(time(NULL));

    do {
        int target = generate_random_number(1, 100);
        int guess_count = 0;
        int user_guess;

        printf("Try to guess my number!\\n");

        do {
            user_guess = get_user_guess();
            guess_count++;

            if (user_guess == target) {
                printf("🎉 Congratulations! You guessed it in %d attempts!\\n", guess_count);
            } else {
                display_hint(user_guess, target);
            }
        } while (user_guess != target);

    } while (play_again());

    printf("\\nThanks for playing! 👋\\n");
    return 0;
}

int generate_random_number(int min, int max) {
    return rand() % (max - min + 1) + min;
}

int get_user_guess(void) {
    int guess;
    int valid_input = 0;

    do {
        printf("Enter your guess (1-100): ");
        if (scanf("%d", &guess) == 1) {
            if (guess >= 1 && guess <= 100) {
                valid_input = 1;
            } else {
                printf("❌ Please enter a number between 1 and 100.\\n");
            }
        } else {
            printf("❌ Invalid input. Please enter a number.\\n");
            // Clear invalid input from buffer
            while (getchar() != '\\n');
        }
    } while (!valid_input);

    return guess;
}

void display_hint(int guess, int target) {
    int difference = abs(guess - target);

    if (difference <= 5) {
        printf("🔥 Very hot! ");
    } else if (difference <= 15) {
        printf("🌡️ Hot! ");
    } else if (difference <= 30) {
        printf("😊 Warm! ");
    } else {
        printf("❄️ Cold! ");
    }

    if (guess < target) {
        printf("Try higher!\\n");
    } else {
        printf("Try lower!\\n");
    }
}

bool play_again(void) {
    char response;
    printf("\\nWould you like to play again? (y/n): ");

    // Clear any remaining input
    while (getchar() != '\\n');

    response = getchar();

    return (response == 'y' || response == 'Y');
}
```#

## Project 2: Simple Calculator

**Description:** A command-line calculator that performs basic arithmetic operations with input validation and history tracking.

**Concepts Used:**
- Functions and modular design
- Arrays and dynamic memory
- String processing
- Error handling
- Switch statements

**Features:**
- Basic arithmetic operations (+, -, *, /)
- Input validation and error handling
- Operation history
- Memory functions (store/recall)
- Clear and exit commands

``` 🔧 Implementation Guide

**Command Parsing Strategy:**
```
// Parse expressions like "5 + 3"
double num1, num2;
char operator;
if (sscanf(input, "%lf %c %lf", &num1, &operator, &num2) == 3) {
    // Valid expression
} else {
    // Handle as command or invalid input
}
```
**Benefits:** Simple parsing for basic expressions, easy to extend.

**History Management:**
```
#define MAX_HISTORY 100
static char *history[MAX_HISTORY];
static int history_count = 0;

// Store successful calculations
if (history_count < MAX_HISTORY) {
    history[history_count++] = strdup(input);
}
```
**Considerations:** Memory management, circular buffer for large histories.

**Command System Design:**
```
// Function-based command handling
bool process_command(char *input) {
    if (strcmp(input, "exit") == 0) {
        return false; // Signal exit
    } else if (strcmp(input, "history") == 0) {
        display_history();
        return true;
    }
    // ... more commands
    return false; // Not a command
}
```
**Advantages:** Clean separation of commands from calculations, extensible.

**Error Handling Patterns:**
```
// Division by zero check
if (operator == '/' && num2 == 0) {
    printf("❌ Division by zero!\\n");
    return;
}
```
**Best Practice:** Validate inputs before operations, provide clear error messages.

```#
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <ctype.h>
#include <stdbool.h>

#define MAX_HISTORY 100
#define MAX_EXPRESSION 100

// Calculator history entry
typedef struct {
    char expression[MAX_EXPRESSION];
    double result;
} HistoryEntry;

// Global calculator state
static HistoryEntry history[MAX_HISTORY];
static int history_count = 0;
static double memory = 0.0;

// Function prototypes
double calculate(double num1, double num2, char operator);
bool is_valid_operator(char op);
void display_history(void);
void display_help(void);
bool process_command(char *input);

int main() {
    char input[MAX_EXPRESSION];

    printf("🧮 Simple Calculator\\n");
    printf("Type 'help' for available commands or 'exit' to quit.\\n\\n");

    while (true) {
        printf("> ");
        if (fgets(input, sizeof(input), stdin) == NULL) {
            break;
        }

        // Remove trailing newline
        input[strcspn(input, "\\n")] = 0;

        // Skip empty input
        if (strlen(input) == 0) {
            continue;
        }

        // Process commands
        if (process_command(input)) {
            continue;
        }

        // Parse arithmetic expression (simplified: num1 op num2)
        double num1, num2;
        char operator;

        if (sscanf(input, "%lf %c %lf", &num1, &operator, &num2) == 3) {
            if (is_valid_operator(operator)) {
                double result = calculate(num1, num2, operator);

                // Add to history
                if (history_count < MAX_HISTORY) {
                    strcpy(history[history_count].expression, input);
                    history[history_count].result = result;
                    history_count++;
                }

                printf("= %.6f\\n", result);
            } else {
                printf("❌ Invalid operator. Use +, -, *, or /\\n");
            }
        } else {
            printf("❌ Invalid expression. Use format: number operator number\\n");
            printf("Example: 5 + 3\\n");
        }
    }

    printf("\\nGoodbye! 👋\\n");
    return 0;
}

double calculate(double num1, double num2, char operator) {
    switch (operator) {
        case '+': return num1 + num2;
        case '-': return num1 - num2;
        case '*': return num1 * num2;
        case '/':
            if (num2 == 0) {
                printf("❌ Division by zero!\\n");
                return 0.0;
            }
            return num1 / num2;
        default:
            return 0.0;
    }
}

bool is_valid_operator(char op) {
    return (op == '+' || op == '-' || op == '*' || op == '/');
}

void display_history(void) {
    if (history_count == 0) {
        printf("No calculations in history.\\n");
        return;
    }

    printf("\\n📜 Calculation History:\\n");
    for (int i = 0; i < history_count; i++) {
        printf("%d. %s = %.6f\\n", i + 1,
               history[i].expression, history[i].result);
    }
    printf("\\n");
}

void display_help(void) {
    printf("\\n🆘 Available Commands:\\n");
    printf("  help          - Show this help message\\n");
    printf("  history       - Show calculation history\\n");
    printf("  clear         - Clear calculation history\\n");
    printf("  mem           - Display memory value\\n");
    printf("  mem = <num>   - Store number in memory\\n");
    printf("  exit          - Exit the calculator\\n");
    printf("\\nArithmetic Operations:\\n");
    printf("  +  Addition\\n");
    printf("  -  Subtraction\\n");
    printf("  *  Multiplication\\n");
    printf("  /  Division\\n");
    printf("\\nExample: 5 + 3\\n\\n");
}

bool process_command(char *input) {
    // Convert to lowercase for case-insensitive comparison
    for (char *p = input; *p; p++) {
        *p = tolower(*p);
    }

    if (strcmp(input, "help") == 0) {
        display_help();
        return true;
    } else if (strcmp(input, "history") == 0) {
        display_history();
        return true;
    } else if (strcmp(input, "clear") == 0) {
        history_count = 0;
        printf("History cleared.\\n");
        return true;
    } else if (strcmp(input, "exit") == 0) {
        return false; // Signal to exit main loop
    } else if (strcmp(input, "mem") == 0) {
        printf("Memory: %.6f\\n", memory);
        return true;
    } else if (strncmp(input, "mem = ", 6) == 0) {
        double value;
        if (sscanf(input + 6, "%lf", &value) == 1) {
            memory = value;
            printf("Stored %.6f in memory.\\n", value);
        } else {
            printf("❌ Invalid memory assignment.\\n");
        }
        return true;
    }

    return false; // Not a command, process as arithmetic expression
}
```#

## Project 3: Student Grade Management System

**Description:** A simple console-based application for managing student grades with file storage capabilities.

**Concepts Used:**
- Structures and data organization
- Dynamic memory allocation
- File I/O operations
- Arrays and searching
- String manipulation

**Features:**
- Add/remove students and grades
- Calculate averages and statistics
- Save/load data to/from files
- Search and sort functionality
- Grade validation and error handling

``` 🔧 Implementation Guide

**Data Structure Design:**
```
typedef struct {
    char name[50];
    int id;
    double grades[10];
    int grade_count;
    double average;
} Student;
```
**Considerations:** Fixed-size arrays for simplicity, expandable to dynamic arrays.

**File I/O Strategy:**
```
// Binary file format for data persistence
void save_students(const Student *students, int count, const char *filename) {
    FILE *file = fopen(filename, "wb");
    if (!file) return;

    fwrite(&count, sizeof(int), 1, file);
    fwrite(students, sizeof(Student), count, file);
    fclose(file);
}
```
**Benefits:** Efficient storage, preserves exact data representation.

**Search and Sort Algorithms:**
```
// Linear search for student by ID
Student *find_student(Student *students, int count, int id) {
    for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {
        if (students[i].id == id) {
            return &students[i];
        }
    }
    return NULL;
}

// Bubble sort by average (descending)
void sort_by_average(Student *students, int count) {
    for (int i = 0; i < count - 1; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < count - i - 1; j++) {
            if (students[j].average < students[j + 1].average) {
                // Swap students
                Student temp = students[j];
                students[j] = students[j + 1];
                students[j + 1] = temp;
            }
        }
    }
}
```
**Performance Notes:** O(n²) sorting acceptable for small datasets.

**Menu-Driven Interface:**
```
typedef enum {
    MENU_ADD_STUDENT = 1,
    MENU_ADD_GRADE,
    MENU_DISPLAY_ALL,
    MENU_CALCULATE_AVERAGES,
    MENU_SAVE_DATA,
    MENU_LOAD_DATA,
    MENU_EXIT
} MenuOption;

// Main menu loop
do {
    display_menu();
    scanf("%d", &choice);
    while (getchar() != '\\n'); // Clear input buffer

    switch (choice) {
        case MENU_ADD_STUDENT:
            add_student(&system);
            break;
        // ... other cases
    }
} while (choice != MENU_EXIT);
```
**UI/UX Tip:** Clear menu options, input validation, consistent formatting.

**Grade Validation:**
```
bool is_valid_grade(double grade) {
    return grade >= 0.0 && grade <= 100.0;
}

// Usage in add_grade function
if (!is_valid_grade(grade)) {
    printf("❌ Grade must be between 0 and 100.\\n");
    return;
}
```
**Data Integrity:** Validate all inputs before storage.

```#
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <ctype.h>
#include <stdbool.h>

#define MAX_NAME_LENGTH 50
#define MAX_STUDENTS 100
#define GRADES_FILE "grades.txt"

// Student structure
typedef struct {
    char name[MAX_NAME_LENGTH];
    int id;
    double grades[10];  // Up to 10 grades per student
    int grade_count;
    double average;
} Student;

// Grade management system
typedef struct {
    Student students[MAX_STUDENTS];
    int student_count;
    char filename[MAX_NAME_LENGTH];
} GradeSystem;

// Function prototypes
void initialize_system(GradeSystem *system, const char *filename);
void display_menu(void);
void add_student(GradeSystem *system);
void add_grade(GradeSystem *system);
void display_students(const GradeSystem *system);
void calculate_averages(GradeSystem *system);
void save_grades(const GradeSystem *system);
void load_grades(GradeSystem *system);
Student *find_student_by_id(GradeSystem *system, int id);
void sort_students_by_average(GradeSystem *system);

int main() {
    GradeSystem system;
    initialize_system(&system, GRADES_FILE);

    // Try to load existing data
    load_grades(&system);

    int choice;
    bool running = true;

    printf("🎓 Student Grade Management System\\n\\n");

    while (running) {
        display_menu();
        printf("Enter your choice: ");
        scanf("%d", &choice);

        // Clear input buffer
        while (getchar() != '\\n');

        switch (choice) {
            case 1:
                add_student(&system);
                break;
            case 2:
                add_grade(&system);
                break;
            case 3:
                display_students(&system);
                break;
            case 4:
                calculate_averages(&system);
                display_students(&system);
                break;
            case 5:
                save_grades(&system);
                break;
            case 6:
                load_grades(&system);
                break;
            case 7:
                sort_students_by_average(&system);
                display_students(&system);
                break;
            case 8:
                printf("Saving data...\\n");
                save_grades(&system);
                running = false;
                break;
            default:
                printf("❌ Invalid choice. Please try again.\\n");
        }
        printf("\\n");
    }

    printf("Goodbye! 👋\\n");
    return 0;
}

void initialize_system(GradeSystem *system, const char *filename) {
    system->student_count = 0;
    strcpy(system->filename, filename);
}

void display_menu(void) {
    printf("📋 Menu:\\n");
    printf("1. Add Student\\n");
    printf("2. Add Grade to Student\\n");
    printf("3. Display All Students\\n");
    printf("4. Calculate Averages\\n");
    printf("5. Save Grades\\n");
    printf("6. Load Grades\\n");
    printf("7. Sort by Average\\n");
    printf("8. Exit\\n");
}

void add_student(GradeSystem *system) {
    if (system->student_count >= MAX_STUDENTS) {
        printf("❌ Maximum number of students reached.\\n");
        return;
    }

    Student *student = &system->students[system->student_count];

    printf("Enter student name: ");
    fgets(student->name, sizeof(student->name), stdin);
    student->name[strcspn(student->name, "\\n")] = 0; // Remove newline

    // Generate simple ID based on student count
    student->id = system->student_count + 1;
    student->grade_count = 0;
    student->average = 0.0;

    system->student_count++;
    printf("✅ Student '%s' added with ID %d.\\n", student->name, student->id);
}

void add_grade(GradeSystem *system) {
    int id;
    printf("Enter student ID: ");
    scanf("%d", &choice);

    Student *student = find_student_by_id(system, id);
    if (!student) {
        printf("❌ Student with ID %d not found.\\n", id);
        return;
    }

    if (student->grade_count >= 10) {
        printf("❌ Maximum grades reached for this student.\\n");
        return;
    }

    double grade;
    printf("Enter grade (0-100): ");
    scanf("%lf", &grade);

    if (grade < 0 || grade > 100) {
        printf("❌ Invalid grade. Must be between 0 and 100.\\n");
        return;
    }

    student->grades[student->grade_count++] = grade;
    printf("✅ Grade %.2f added to %s.\\n", grade, student->name);
}

void display_students(const GradeSystem *system) {
    if (system->student_count == 0) {
        printf("📝 No students in the system.\\n");
        return;
    }

    printf("\\n📊 Student Information:\\n");
    printf("%-5s %-20s %-10s %-15s\\n", "ID", "Name", "Grades", "Average");
    printf("----- -------------------- ---------- ---------------\\n");

    for (int i = 0; i < system->student_count; i++) {
        const Student *student = &system->students[i];

        printf("%-5d %-20s ", student->id, student->name);

        if (student->grade_count > 0) {
            printf("%d grades", student->grade_count);
        } else {
            printf("No grades");
        }

        printf("   %.2f\\n", student->average);
    }
}

void calculate_averages(GradeSystem *system) {
    for (int i = 0; i < system->student_count; i++) {
        Student *student = &system->students[i];

        if (student->grade_count > 0) {
            double sum = 0.0;
            for (int j = 0; j < student->grade_count; j++) {
                sum += student->grades[j];
            }
            student->average = sum / student->grade_count;
        } else {
            student->average = 0.0;
        }
    }
    printf("✅ Averages calculated.\\n");
}

void save_grades(const GradeSystem *system) {
    FILE *file = fopen(system->filename, "w");
    if (!file) {
        perror("❌ Failed to open file for saving");
        return;
    }

    fprintf(file, "%d\\n", system->student_count);

    for (int i = 0; i < system->student_count; i++) {
        const Student *student = &system->students[i];

        fprintf(file, "%d\\n%s\\n%d\\n",
                student->id, student->name, student->grade_count);

        for (int j = 0; j < student->grade_count; j++) {
            fprintf(file, "%.2f\\n", student->grades[j]);
        }
    }

    fclose(file);
    printf("✅ Grades saved to %s.\\n", system->filename);
}

void load_grades(GradeSystem *system) {
    FILE *file = fopen(system->filename, "r");
    if (!file) {
        printf("ℹ️ No existing grade file found.\\n");
        return;
    }

    fscanf(file, "%d", &system->student_count);

    for (int i = 0; i < system->student_count; i++) {
        Student *student = &system->students[i];

        fscanf(file, "%d", &student->id);

        // Read name (handle spaces)
        fgetc(file); // consume newline
        fgets(student->name, sizeof(student->name), file);
        student->name[strcspn(student->name, "\\n")] = 0;

        fscanf(file, "%d", &student->grade_count);

        for (int j = 0; j < student->grade_count; j++) {
            fscanf(file, "%lf", &student->grades[j]);
        }
    }

    fclose(file);
    calculate_averages(system);
    printf("✅ Grades loaded from %s.\\n", system->filename);
}

Student *find_student_by_id(GradeSystem *system, int id) {
    for (int i = 0; i < system->student_count; i++) {
        if (system->students[i].id == id) {
            return &system->students[i];
        }
    }
    return NULL;
}

void sort_students_by_average(GradeSystem *system) {
    for (int i = 0; i < system->student_count - 1; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < system->student_count - i - 1; j++) {
            if (system->students[j].average < system->students[j + 1].average) {
                // Swap students (descending order - highest average first)
                Student temp = system->students[j];
                system->students[j] = system->students[j + 1];
                system->students[j + 1] = temp;
            }
        }
    }
    printf("✅ Students sorted by average (highest first).\\n");
}
```#

## Project 4: Text File Analyzer

**Description:** A utility program that analyzes text files and provides statistics about word usage, character frequency, and readability metrics.

**Concepts Used:**
- File I/O operations
- String processing and tokenization
- Dynamic memory allocation
- Arrays and data structures
- Command-line argument parsing

**Features:**
- Word count and frequency analysis
- Character and line statistics
- Readability metrics (Flesch Reading Ease)
- Most common words display
- Case-insensitive analysis options

``` 🔧 Implementation Guide

**File Reading Strategy:**
```
// Efficient file processing with buffering
FILE *file = fopen(filename, "r");
if (!file) {
    perror("Failed to open file");
    return NULL;
}

char buffer[4096];
while (fgets(buffer, sizeof(buffer), file)) {
    // Process each line
    process_line(buffer);
}
fclose(file);
```
**Benefits:** Memory-efficient, handles large files, automatic buffering.

**Word Tokenization:**
```
// Extract words from text using delimiters
char *token = strtok(line, " \\t\\n\\r.,;:!?\"'()[]{}");
while (token) {
    // Process word
    process_word(token);
    token = strtok(NULL, " \\t\\n\\r.,;:!?\"'()[]{}");
}
```
**Edge Cases:** Handle punctuation, multiple spaces, special characters.

**Word Frequency Hashing:**
```
// Simple hash table for word frequencies
#define HASH_SIZE 10007
typedef struct {
    char *word;
    int count;
} WordEntry;

WordEntry *hash_table[HASH_SIZE];

// DJB2 hash function for strings
unsigned long hash_word(const char *str) {
    unsigned long hash = 5381;
    int c;
    while ((c = *str++)) {
        hash = ((hash << 5) + hash) + c;
    }
    return hash % HASH_SIZE;
}
```
**Performance:** O(1) average lookup, handles hash collisions.

**Readability Calculations:**
```
// Flesch Reading Ease Score
double calculate_readability(int words, int sentences, int syllables) {
    if (sentences == 0 || words == 0) return 0.0;
    double avg_words_per_sentence = (double)words / sentences;
    double avg_syllables_per_word = (double)syllables / words;
    return 206.835 - 1.015 * avg_words_per_sentence - 84.6 * avg_syllables_per_word;
}
```
**Formula:** Based on standard readability metrics, returns score 0-100.

**Command-Line Argument Handling:**
```
// Simple argument parsing
int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
    if (argc < 2) {
        fprintf(stderr, "Usage: %s <filename> [options]\\n", argv[0]);
        return 1;
    }

    const char *filename = argv[1];
    bool case_sensitive = false;

    for (int i = 2; i < argc; i++) {
        if (strcmp(argv[i], "--case-sensitive") == 0) {
            case_sensitive = true;
        }
    }
    // ... process file
}
```
**Extensibility:** Easy to add more command-line options.

```#
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <ctype.h>
#include <stdbool.h>

#define MAX_WORD_LENGTH 100
#define MAX_WORDS 10000

// Word frequency structure
typedef struct {
    char word[MAX_WORD_LENGTH];
    int count;
} WordFreq;

// Text analysis results
typedef struct {
    int total_characters;
    int total_words;
    int total_lines;
    int unique_words;
    double average_word_length;
    double readability_score;
    WordFreq *word_frequencies;
    int word_freq_count;
} TextAnalysis;

// Function prototypes
TextAnalysis *analyze_text_file(const char *filename, bool case_sensitive);
void free_text_analysis(TextAnalysis *analysis);
void display_analysis(const TextAnalysis *analysis);
int compare_word_freq(const void *a, const void *b);
double calculate_readability_score(int total_words, int total_sentences, int total_syllables);
int count_syllables(const char *word);

int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
    if (argc < 2) {
        printf("Usage: %s <filename> [case-sensitive]\\n", argv[0]);
        printf("  case-sensitive: 1 for case-sensitive analysis, 0 for case-insensitive (default)\\n");
        return 1;
    }

    const char *filename = argv[1];
    bool case_sensitive = false;

    if (argc >= 3) {
        case_sensitive = atoi(argv[2]) != 0;
    }

    printf("📄 Analyzing file: %s\\n", filename);
    printf("Case %ssensitive analysis\\n", case_sensitive ? "" : "in");

    TextAnalysis *analysis = analyze_text_file(filename, case_sensitive);
    if (!analysis) {
        fprintf(stderr, "❌ Failed to analyze file\\n");
        return 1;
    }

    display_analysis(analysis);
    free_text_analysis(analysis);

    return 0;
}

TextAnalysis *analyze_text_file(const char *filename, bool case_sensitive) {
    FILE *file = fopen(filename, "r");
    if (!file) {
        perror("Failed to open file");
        return NULL;
    }

    TextAnalysis *analysis = calloc(1, sizeof(TextAnalysis));
    if (!analysis) {
        fclose(file);
        return NULL;
    }

    analysis->word_frequencies = calloc(MAX_WORDS, sizeof(WordFreq));
    if (!analysis->word_frequencies) {
        free(analysis);
        fclose(file);
        return NULL;
    }

    char line[1024];
    char word[MAX_WORD_LENGTH];
    int total_syllables = 0;

    while (fgets(line, sizeof(line), file)) {
        analysis->total_lines++;
        analysis->total_characters += strlen(line);

        // Tokenize line into words
        char *token = strtok(line, " \\t\\n\\r.,;:!?\"'()[]{}");
        while (token) {
            // Copy and normalize word
            strcpy(word, token);
            if (!case_sensitive) {
                for (char *p = word; *p; p++) {
                    *p = tolower(*p);
                }
            }

            // Remove non-alphabetic characters from word boundaries
            size_t len = strlen(word);
            while (len > 0 && !isalpha(word[len - 1])) {
                word[--len] = '\\0';
            }

            size_t start = 0;
            while (start < len && !isalpha(word[start])) {
                start++;
            }

            if (start < len) {
                // Valid word
                char clean_word[MAX_WORD_LENGTH];
                strcpy(clean_word, word + start);

                analysis->total_words++;
                analysis->average_word_length += strlen(clean_word);
                total_syllables += count_syllables(clean_word);

                // Update word frequency
                bool found = false;
                for (int i = 0; i < analysis->word_freq_count; i++) {
                    if (strcmp(analysis->word_frequencies[i].word, clean_word) == 0) {
                        analysis->word_frequencies[i].count++;
                        found = true;
                        break;
                    }
                }

                if (!found && analysis->word_freq_count < MAX_WORDS) {
                    strcpy(analysis->word_frequencies[analysis->word_freq_count].word, clean_word);
                    analysis->word_frequencies[analysis->word_freq_count].count = 1;
                    analysis->word_freq_count++;
                }
            }

            token = strtok(NULL, " \\t\\n\\r.,;:!?\"'()[]{}");
        }
    }

    fclose(file);

    // Calculate final statistics
    if (analysis->total_words > 0) {
        analysis->average_word_length /= analysis->total_words;
    }

    analysis->unique_words = analysis->word_freq_count;

    // Estimate sentences (rough approximation)
    int estimated_sentences = analysis->total_lines / 2;
    if (estimated_sentences == 0) estimated_sentences = 1;

    analysis->readability_score = calculate_readability_score(
        analysis->total_words, estimated_sentences, total_syllables);

    // Sort word frequencies (most common first)
    qsort(analysis->word_frequencies, analysis->word_freq_count,
          sizeof(WordFreq), compare_word_freq);

    return analysis;
}

void free_text_analysis(TextAnalysis *analysis) {
    if (analysis) {
        free(analysis->word_frequencies);
        free(analysis);
    }
}

void display_analysis(const TextAnalysis *analysis) {
    printf("\\n📊 Text Analysis Results:\\n");
    printf("════════════════════════════════════════\\n");
    printf("📝 Total Characters: %d\\n", analysis->total_characters);
    printf("📝 Total Words: %d\\n", analysis->total_words);
    printf("📝 Total Lines: %d\\n", analysis->total_lines);
    printf("📝 Unique Words: %d\\n", analysis->unique_words);
    printf("📝 Average Word Length: %.2f characters\\n", analysis->average_word_length);
    printf("📖 Readability Score: %.1f (Flesch Reading Ease)\\n", analysis->readability_score);

    if (analysis->readability_score >= 90) {
        printf("   Difficulty Level: Very Easy\\n");
    } else if (analysis->readability_score >= 80) {
        printf("   Difficulty Level: Easy\\n");
    } else if (analysis->readability_score >= 70) {
        printf("   Difficulty Level: Fairly Easy\\n");
    } else if (analysis->readability_score >= 60) {
        printf("   Difficulty Level: Standard\\n");
    } else if (analysis->readability_score >= 50) {
        printf("   Difficulty Level: Fairly Difficult\\n");
    } else if (analysis->readability_score >= 30) {
        printf("   Difficulty Level: Difficult\\n");
    } else {
        printf("   Difficulty Level: Very Difficult\\n");
    }

    printf("\\n🔝 Most Common Words:\\n");
    printf("────────────────────\\n");

    int display_count = analysis->word_freq_count < 20 ? analysis->word_freq_count : 20;
    for (int i = 0; i < display_count; i++) {
        printf("%2d. %-15s (%d occurrences)\\n",
               i + 1,
               analysis->word_frequencies[i].word,
               analysis->word_frequencies[i].count);
    }
}

int compare_word_freq(const void *a, const void *b) {
    const WordFreq *freq_a = (const WordFreq *)a;
    const WordFreq *freq_b = (const WordFreq *)b;
    return freq_b->count - freq_a->count; // Descending order
}

double calculate_readability_score(int total_words, int total_sentences, int total_syllables) {
    if (total_sentences == 0 || total_words == 0) return 0.0;

    // Flesch Reading Ease formula
    // 206.835 - 1.015 * (words/sentences) - 84.6 * (syllables/words)
    double avg_words_per_sentence = (double)total_words / total_sentences;
    double avg_syllables_per_word = (double)total_syllables / total_words;

    return 206.835 - 1.015 * avg_words_per_sentence - 84.6 * avg_syllables_per_word;
}

int count_syllables(const char *word) {
    int count = 0;
    bool in_vowel_group = false;

    for (const char *p = word; *p; p++) {
        char c = tolower(*p);
        bool is_vowel = (c == 'a' || c == 'e' || c == 'i' || c == 'o' || c == 'u' || c == 'y');

        if (is_vowel && !in_vowel_group) {
            count++;
            in_vowel_group = true;
        } else if (!is_vowel) {
            in_vowel_group = false;
        }
    }

    // Every word has at least one syllable
    return count > 0 ? count : 1;
}
```#

## Project 5: Simple Task Manager (Todo List)

**Description:** A command-line task management application with persistent storage using file I/O.

**Concepts Used:**
- Linked lists for dynamic data structures
- File I/O for data persistence
- Date and time handling
- String parsing and validation
- Memory management

**Features:**
- Add, remove, and update tasks
- Task priorities and due dates
- Mark tasks as completed
- Save/load tasks to/from files
- Filter and search functionality

``` 🔧 Implementation Guide

**Linked List Data Structure:**
```
typedef struct Task {
    int id;
    char description[200];
    bool completed;
    time_t created_at;
    time_t due_date;
    struct Task *next;
} Task;

typedef struct {
    Task *head;
    int count;
} TaskList;
```
**Advantages:** Dynamic size, easy insertion/deletion, O(1) operations at ends.

**File Persistence Format:**
```
// Binary serialization for efficiency
void save_tasks(const TaskList *list, const char *filename) {
    FILE *file = fopen(filename, "wb");
    if (!file) return;

    Task *current = list->head;
    while (current) {
        fwrite(current, sizeof(Task), 1, file);
        current = current->next;
    }
    fclose(file);
}
```
**Note:** This saves the linked list structure directly. For production, consider a more robust format.

**Task Search and Filtering:**
```
Task *find_task_by_id(TaskList *list, int id) {
    Task *current = list->head;
    while (current) {
        if (current->id == id) {
            return current;
        }
        current = current->next;
    }
    return NULL;
}

Task **filter_completed_tasks(TaskList *list, int *count) {
    Task **filtered = malloc(sizeof(Task *) * list->count);
    *count = 0;

    Task *current = list->head;
    while (current) {
        if (current->completed) {
            filtered[(*count)++] = current;
        }
        current = current->next;
    }

    return filtered;
}
```
**Performance:** O(n) search, consider hash table for large task lists.

**Date and Time Handling:**
```
#include <time.h>

// Get current time
time_t now = time(NULL);

// Format for display
char *format_time(time_t timestamp) {
    static char buffer[20];
    struct tm *time_info = localtime(&timestamp);
    strftime(buffer, sizeof(buffer), "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M", time_info);
    return buffer;
}
```
**Cross-Platform:** #()# and #()# work on most systems.

**Memory Management:**
```
void free_task_list(TaskList *list) {
    Task *current = list->head;
    while (current) {
        Task *next = current->next;
        free(current);
        current = next;
    }
    list->head = NULL;
    list->count = 0;
}
```
**Critical:** Always free allocated memory to prevent leaks.

```#
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <time.h>
#include <stdbool.h>

#define MAX_TASK_LENGTH 200
#define TASKS_FILE "tasks.txt"

// Task priority levels
typedef enum {
    PRIORITY_LOW,
    PRIORITY_MEDIUM,
    PRIORITY_HIGH,
    PRIORITY_URGENT
} Priority;

// Task structure
typedef struct Task {
    int id;
    char description[MAX_TASK_LENGTH];
    Priority priority;
    time_t created_time;
    time_t due_time;
    bool completed;
    struct Task *next;
} Task;

// Task manager
typedef struct {
    Task *head;
    int next_id;
    char filename[MAX_TASK_LENGTH];
} TaskManager;

// Function prototypes
void task_manager_init(TaskManager *manager, const char *filename);
void task_manager_destroy(TaskManager *manager);
void add_task(TaskManager *manager, const char *description, Priority priority, time_t due_time);
void remove_task(TaskManager *manager, int id);
void mark_completed(TaskManager *manager, int id);
void display_tasks(const TaskManager *manager);
void display_task(const Task *task);
void save_tasks(const TaskManager *manager);
void load_tasks(TaskManager *manager);
Task *find_task(TaskManager *manager, int id);
const char *priority_string(Priority priority);
const char *format_time(time_t timestamp);
void display_menu(void);

int main() {
    TaskManager manager;
    task_manager_init(&manager, TASKS_FILE);

    // Load existing tasks
    load_tasks(&manager);

    printf("📋 Simple Task Manager\\n\\n");

    bool running = true;
    while (running) {
        display_menu();

        int choice;
        printf("Enter your choice: ");
        scanf("%d", &choice);

        // Clear input buffer
        while (getchar() != '\\n');

        switch (choice) {
            case 1: {
                char description[MAX_TASK_LENGTH];
                int priority_choice;
                time_t due_time = 0;

                printf("Enter task description: ");
                fgets(description, sizeof(description), stdin);
                description[strcspn(description, "\\n")] = 0;

                printf("Select priority (0=Low, 1=Medium, 2=High, 3=Urgent): ");
                scanf("%d", &priority_choice);
                while (getchar() != '\\n'); // Clear buffer

                if (priority_choice < PRIORITY_LOW || priority_choice > PRIORITY_URGENT) {
                    priority_choice = PRIORITY_MEDIUM;
                }

                add_task(&manager, description, (Priority)priority_choice, due_time);
                printf("✅ Task added!\\n");
                break;
            }
            case 2: {
                int id;
                printf("Enter task ID to remove: ");
                scanf("%d", &id);
                while (getchar() != '\\n'); // Clear buffer

                remove_task(&manager, id);
                break;
            }
            case 3: {
                int id;
                printf("Enter task ID to mark as completed: ");
                scanf("%d", &id);
                while (getchar() != '\\n'); // Clear buffer

                mark_completed(&manager, id);
                break;
            }
            case 4:
                display_tasks(&manager);
                break;
            case 5:
                save_tasks(&manager);
                break;
            case 6:
                load_tasks(&manager);
                break;
            case 7:
                printf("Saving tasks...\\n");
                save_tasks(&manager);
                running = false;
                break;
            default:
                printf("❌ Invalid choice. Please try again.\\n");
        }
        printf("\\n");
    }

    task_manager_destroy(&manager);
    printf("Goodbye! 👋\\n");

    return 0;
}

void task_manager_init(TaskManager *manager, const char *filename) {
    manager->head = NULL;
    manager->next_id = 1;
    strcpy(manager->filename, filename);
}

void task_manager_destroy(TaskManager *manager) {
    Task *current = manager->head;
    while (current) {
        Task *next = current->next;
        free(current);
        current = next;
    }
    manager->head = NULL;
}

void add_task(TaskManager *manager, const char *description, Priority priority, time_t due_time) {
    Task *new_task = malloc(sizeof(Task));
    if (!new_task) {
        printf("❌ Failed to allocate memory for task\\n");
        return;
    }

    new_task->id = manager->next_id++;
    strcpy(new_task->description, description);
    new_task->priority = priority;
    new_task->created_time = time(NULL);
    new_task->due_time = due_time;
    new_task->completed = false;
    new_task->next = NULL;

    // Add to end of list
    if (manager->head == NULL) {
        manager->head = new_task;
    } else {
        Task *current = manager->head;
        while (current->next) {
            current = current->next;
        }
        current->next = new_task;
    }
}

void remove_task(TaskManager *manager, int id) {
    Task *current = manager->head;
    Task *previous = NULL;

    while (current) {
        if (current->id == id) {
            if (previous) {
                previous->next = current->next;
            } else {
                manager->head = current->next;
            }
            free(current);
            printf("✅ Task %d removed\\n", id);
            return;
        }
        previous = current;
        current = current->next;
    }

    printf("❌ Task %d not found\\n", id);
}

void mark_completed(TaskManager *manager, int id) {
    Task *task = find_task(manager, id);
    if (task) {
        task->completed = true;
        printf("✅ Task %d marked as completed\\n", id);
    } else {
        printf("❌ Task %d not found\\n", id);
    }
}

void display_tasks(const TaskManager *manager) {
    if (manager->head == NULL) {
        printf("📝 No tasks found\\n");
        return;
    }

    printf("\\n📋 Current Tasks:\\n");
    printf("═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\\n");

    Task *current = manager->head;
    while (current) {
        display_task(current);
        current = current->next;
    }
}

void display_task(const Task *task) {
    const char *status = task->completed ? "✅" : "⏳";
    printf("%s [%d] %s\\n", status, task->id, task->description);
    printf("   Priority: %s\\n", priority_string(task->priority));
    printf("   Created: %s\\n", format_time(task->created_time));

    if (task->due_time > 0) {
        printf("   Due: %s\\n", format_time(task->due_time));
    }

    printf("\\n");
}

void save_tasks(const TaskManager *manager) {
    FILE *file = fopen(manager->filename, "w");
    if (!file) {
        perror("❌ Failed to open file for saving");
        return;
    }

    Task *current = manager->head;
    while (current) {
        fprintf(file, "%d\\n%s\\n%d\\n%ld\\n%ld\\n%d\\n",
                current->id,
                current->description,
                (int)current->priority,
                (long)current->created_time,
                (long)current->due_time,
                current->completed ? 1 : 0);
        current = current->next;
    }

    fclose(file);
    printf("✅ Tasks saved to %s\\n", manager->filename);
}

void load_tasks(TaskManager *manager) {
    FILE *file = fopen(manager->filename, "r");
    if (!file) {
        printf("ℹ️ No existing task file found\\n");
        return;
    }

    // Clear existing tasks
    task_manager_destroy(manager);
    task_manager_init(manager, manager->filename);

    int id, priority_int, completed_int;
    char description[MAX_TASK_LENGTH];
    long created_time, due_time;

    while (fscanf(file, "%d", &id) == 1) {
        // Read description (handle multi-line)
        fgetc(file); // consume newline
        fgets(description, sizeof(description), file);
        description[strcspn(description, "\\n")] = 0;

        fscanf(file, "%d", &priority_int);
        fscanf(file, "%ld", &created_time);
        fscanf(file, "%ld", &due_time);
        fscanf(file, "%d", &completed_int);

        // Create task
        Task *task = malloc(sizeof(Task));
        if (task) {
            task->id = id;
            strcpy(task->description, description);
            task->priority = (Priority)priority_int;
            task->created_time = (time_t)created_time;
            task->due_time = (time_t)due_time;
            task->completed = completed_int != 0;
            task->next = NULL;

            // Add to list
            if (manager->head == NULL) {
                manager->head = task;
            } else {
                Task *current = manager->head;
                while (current->next) {
                    current = current->next;
                }
                current->next = task;
            }

            // Update next_id
            if (id >= manager->next_id) {
                manager->next_id = id + 1;
            }
        }
    }

    fclose(file);
    printf("✅ Tasks loaded from %s\\n", manager->filename);
}

Task *find_task(TaskManager *manager, int id) {
    Task *current = manager->head;
    while (current) {
        if (current->id == id) {
            return current;
        }
        current = current->next;
    }
    return NULL;
}

const char *priority_string(Priority priority) {
    switch (priority) {
        case PRIORITY_LOW: return "Low";
        case PRIORITY_MEDIUM: return "Medium";
        case PRIORITY_HIGH: return "High";
        case PRIORITY_URGENT: return "Urgent";
        default: return "Unknown";
    }
}

const char *format_time(time_t timestamp) {
    static char buffer[20];
    struct tm *time_info = localtime(&timestamp);
    strftime(buffer, sizeof(buffer), "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M", time_info);
    return buffer;
}

void display_menu(void) {
    printf("📋 Task Manager Menu:\\n");
    printf("1. Add Task\\n");
    printf("2. Remove Task\\n");
    printf("3. Mark Task as Completed\\n");
    printf("4. Display All Tasks\\n");
    printf("5. Save Tasks\\n");
    printf("6. Load Tasks\\n");
    printf("7. Exit\\nimport { SubLesson } from '../../../../data/lessonsData';

export const topic_18_1: SubLesson = {
